The desk merged reports about dates into #4471 by subject. The export shows two different
causes, so the reports need separate engineering tickets.

## Resolution

The course's engineering update records #4471 as closed on 5 October 2026.
The parser was **fixed** by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
The hint was **won't fix** because the booking-v3 form was retired, not repaired.
The corresponding GitHub tickets are closed as completed and not planned, respectively.
The counts below describe the exported incident, not ongoing failures after closure.

The shared parser reads dates month first, while every affected tenant in this export writes
the day first. Separately, booking-v3 shows a month-first hint even for day-first tenants;
reports sent through that form follow a different failure path.

<Callout kind="warn">
One merged ticket does not mean one problem. Use the tenant and channel to distinguish the
parser failure from the booking-v3 hint failure; the intake tag alone is not reliable.
</Callout>

